solidcraft-render-server

A modified build of SolidCraft v0.47.0 (https://github.com/tangency-labs/solidcraft, tag v0.47.0).
Source of this build: https://github.com/jianzhichun/solidz-render-server

Changes against SolidCraft v0.47.0 (apps/solidcraft-render-server/SPIKE.md lists each one):
- new: apps/solidcraft-render-server (this program: the editing UI drawn offscreen and streamed to
  an embedding host; its brand scan, tests/brand_scan.rs, walks what a user can reach in it)
- moved: the desktop app's control protocol implementation, from apps/solidcraft/src/control_server.rs
  to crates/ui-egui/src/control_protocol.rs
- changed: crates/engine (a process-wide host read-only switch, crates/engine/src/read_only.rs,
  checked in Session::execute; a folder for per-user files, recovery::set_user_dir; a switch
  that refuses problem reports, report_issue::refuse, which this program turns on)
- changed: crates/ui-egui (system fonts shared, not copied; CJK system faces with a line gap drawn
  in the middle of their line; refusals and export status in the interface language; a host hook
  for how status messages read; under a host product's name, no links to SolidCraft's issue
  tracker, documentation, updates or community; commands a host refuses, which this program uses
  to leave out the Assistant and the app bar's tile picker; where a host runs the editor, Export in the Insert tab's
  Import/Export panel)
- changed: crates/ui-text (a host product's name in every message)
- changed: xtask/src/layers.rs (registers the new app), Cargo.lock (the new package),
  THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt (regenerated with cargo xtask licences for this Cargo.lock: url 2.5.9,
  form_urlencoded 1.2.3), and the messages in
  assets/locales/pending/command-refusals-and-export-status.json and
  assets/locales/pending/embedded-import-export.json

Licences are SolidCraft's, unchanged: the code is under the MIT License or the Apache License 2.0
(LICENSE-MIT, LICENSE-APACHE; NOTICE). This program links SolidCraft's UI kit, look and theme, which
are under the SolidCraft Brand and Interface Licence (LICENSE-BRAND). The licences of the third-party
crates built into it are in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt.
